meta {
  name: auth
}

docs {
  Token acquisition requests: OIDC discovery and JWKS (sanity checks that the realm is up and its signing keys are published), then L2 `private_key_jwt` token requests for both demo hospitals (placer/hospital-a, fulfiller/hospital-b), with and without an RFC 9396 `authorization_details` parameter binding the token to a specific FHIR resource (`fhirContext`).
  
  Run this folder first — `validation/` and `negative/` reuse the tokens these requests store in environment variables (`placerL2Token`, `fulfillerL2Token`, `placerContextToken`, `fulfillerContextToken`).
  
  Requires Bruno's Node.js sandbox ("Developer mode" / `--sandbox unsafe`) for the L2 requests' client-assertion signing scripts — see `ai-docs/bruno.md`.
}
